+# Authoritative observation watermark — abstract protocol ↔ runtime
+
+Model: `AuthoritativeObservationWatermark.tla`.
+Quest: `movielens-authoritative-observation-watermark`.
+
+This focused model composes a failed-read retry, successful complete
+authoritative reads, unchanged/confirmed-empty reconciliation, separate
+observation-evidence publication, preflight freshness classification, and
+schema admission.
+
+| Model | Runtime |
+| --- | --- |
+| `FailInitialAuthoritativeRead` / `RequestRepairRetry` | `AdminServiceDiscovery.ensureAuthoritativeDiscoveryCacheRepair` fails closed on incomplete reads and permits a later bounded repair attempt |
+| `CompleteAuthoritativeRead` | `AdminServiceDiscovery.readAuthoritativeSystemTableRows` returns a complete unchanged or confirmed-empty table result |
+| `ReconcileAuthoritativeTruth` | `ControlPlaneSystemTableGateway.reconcileAuthoritativeCacheRows` compares authoritative rows with the local cache without fabricating a CDC mutation |
+| `mutationWatermarkAdvanced` | `SystemTableCache.lastAppliedAtMsByTableName`; it must remain unchanged for a no-op reconcile |
+| `observationWatermarkPublished` | `SystemTableCache.recordAuthoritativeObservation` stores per-table observation time/cause as distinct data |
+| `ClassifyFreshFromPublishedEvidence` | `AdminPreflightSnapshot.buildPreflightCacheFreshnessSummary` selects the newest mutation or authoritative-observation watermark |
+| `AdmitSchema` | the MovieLens schema-admission gate accepts a fresh control snapshot |
+
+The fixed configuration proves that authoritative observation does not invent a
+mutation, freshness and admission require published evidence, and successful
+unchanged/empty repair eventually admits schema. The mutation-only mutant keeps
+the old coupling to last mutation time and violates eventual admission after a
+successful no-op repair.
+
+This is intentionally not a claim that every interaction between repository
+layers is modeled in TLA+ or Alloy.
